                <pb facs="0601" n="531" sameAs="frus:frus1867p2/pg531"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>Mr. Romero to Mr.
                        Seward</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington,</hi>
                        </placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1867-03-16"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 16, 1867</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Sir:</hi> I have the honor to send to you a
                    collection of documents upon the affairs of Mexico, which the French government
                    laid before the legislative body at the opening of its session on the 18th
                    February last past, taken from No. 53 of the Moniteur Universel, corresponding
                    with the 22d of February aforesaid.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>M. ROMERO.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
















